    "content_conclusions": [
      "All 74 fixed-scope file hashes match. The seven-page blessing content and two implementation pages match the reviewed preview exactly.",
      "The map entry, two variants and three bindings are the exact Phosphor Blast Pistol Branx Mk XI (M1), Stub Revolver Zarona Mk IIa (M1), and Stub Revolver Agripinaa Mk XIV (M2) inventory intersection; both weapon reverse indexes link back to the correct Hand Cannon pages.",
      "The two own tier tables show Phosphor +.05/.075/.10/.15 and Stub Revolver +.30/.40/.50/.60 to critical-strike rending. Each actual wrapper clones the held-slot conditional rending-on-critical template; the own same-key tier replaces the fallback rather than adding to it.",
      "Ordinary hip/ADS hit-scan and each configured pistol-whip/follow-up Sweep route use their native critical result. The Phosphor reload-origin Sweep routes remain subject to their real reload transition. Its backblast and burn ticks are noncritical and are correctly excluded; its separate native ranged target-rending effect is distinguished.",
      "The M2 example states far range/dropoff, target_index=1/default target, armored, no target-settings override, lerp inputs .5, and critical-hit conditions. A=.6+.15=.75. With no other rending, armor factor 1 and overdamage .25, B=100 before the armor segment gives I r=.30 ->101.25 and IV r=.60 ->108.75 against same-critical baseline75, a 35%/45% increase in this armor segment only, not final HP damage.",
      "English and Traditional Chinese RAW are paired by the same description hash. The own formatter reconstructs all four tiers for both variants. Omitted attack conditions and armor math are document omissions, not RAW contradictions; no erratum is needed.",
      "The actual icon 118 path and verified attachment are distinct and match the image receipt; the current shared map entry points to that attachment."
    ],
    "review_method": "Reused the already completed candidate content review for unchanged gameplay; verified the exact fixed formal scope, actual candidate-vs-formal page bytes, updated current map/reverse links, and relevant root material receipts."
